after concluding, and, most importantly, the degeneration of re-verification into verbatim loops, which is what actually kills the answers. Copying a line verbatim needs a mechanism that looks up the previous occurrence of the current context and reproduces what followed. In this hybrid model that can be done by the six full-attention layers, or by DeltaNet heads, whose 4-tap causal convolution lets a key encode the previous token so that the head can do associative \"induction\" recall. As a free weight-only step, I'll measure each DeltaNet head's conv-kernel lag profile for its query, key and value channels. Heads whose keys weight the previous token while queries and values weight the current token have the induction signature. That narrows the candidates before I spend a teacher-forced pass, which will show which layers actually push the copied token in real loops.\n\n```python\n# Weight analysis: DeltaNet conv1d lag structure per head (induction signature = keys emphasize lag>=1, queries/values lag 0)\ndef lag_profile(l):\n    w=load(P+f'{l}.linear_attn.conv1d.weight').squeeze(1)  # (6144,4); index 3 = current token (lag0)\n    q=w[:2048].view(16,128,4); k=w[2048:4096].view(16,128,4); v=w[4096:].view(16,128,4)\n    f=lambda x: (x**2).sum(1)/ (x**2).sum((1,2))[:,None]  # (16,4) energy per lag\n    return f(q).numpy()[:,::-1], f(k).numpy()[:,::-1], f(v).numpy()[:,::-1]  # columns now lag0..lag3\nprint('per DeltaNet layer: #heads with k-lag>=1 energy >0.5 & q-lag0 >0.5 ; top heads (k_lag1+, q_lag0)')\nind_scores={}\nfor l in range(24):\n    if l in (3,7,11,15,19,23): continue\n    qp,kp,vp=lag_profile(l)\n    kprev=kp[:,1:].sum(1); q0=qp[:,0]; v0=vp[:,0]\n    score=kprev*q0\n    ind_scores[l]=score\n    top=np.argsort(-score)[:3]\n    print(l, int(((kprev>0.5)&(q0>0.5)).sum()), [(int(h), round(kprev[h],2), round(q0[h],2), round(v0[h],2)) for h in top])\n```","ttft_ms":70333,"type":"result","duration_ms":78462,"uuid":"8f9c8ca2-768a-47d6-a17c-6cc2be01792e","ttft_str